# Compatibility: NAMD uses velocity Verlet, SETTLE plus SHAKE for solute,
# and solute constraints that are not M-SHAKE.
# Engine-native NPT candidate: NAMD Monte Carlo pressure control replaces
# the GENESIS-like Langevin piston and uses its documented 50-step default.
# This route is benchmarked separately and is not assumed faster a priori.
amber on
oldParmReader off
parmfile ../../data/variants/factorix/native_archive_amber_factorix_3site/system.prmtop
ambercoor ../../data/variants/factorix/native_archive_amber_factorix_3site/system.inpcrd
readexclusions yes
exclude scaled1-4
oneFourScaling 0.8333333333333334
scnb 2
cellBasisVector1 142.0855468 0 0
cellBasisVector2 0 83.3368905 0
cellBasisVector3 0 0 78.6783548
cellOrigin 71.0427734 41.66844525 39.3391774
wrapAll on
cutoff 9
switching off
switchdist 9
pairlistdist 11
PME yes
PMEGridSpacing 1.0
PMETolerance 1.0e-5
zeroMomentum no
GPUresident on
nonbondedFreq 1
fullElectFrequency 1
timestep 2
rigidBonds all
useSettle on
seed 314159
temperature 300
outputName factorix__npt__2fs__native
outputEnergies 1000
outputTiming 1000
DCDfreq 0
restartfreq 0
XSTFreq 0
stochRescale on
stochRescaleTemp 300
stochRescalePeriod 5
stochRescaleFreq 10
MonteCarloPressure on
